{
  "version": 1,
  "readme": [
    "ae-landscape — the machine with the drums taken out (manual ch. 55).",
    "",
    "Two pads run free: `tape` (five triangles at 432Hz, drifting only in colour)",
    "and `atmo` (the Deep Pad — forty-second attack, sinking slowly, struck by the",
    "sparse crack and modal hits). Both go through `pads` (Breathe). A held",
    "`drone` holds the middle. Four effects feed each other through `fbm`; the",
    "notverb jumper throws freezes; `terra` moves one thing at a time at walking",
    "pace; `warp` stretches the clock now and then. The mix feeds `loop` (a",
    "looper whose playhead follows a staircase curve) into `oxide`.",
    "Nothing appears for about thirty seconds. That's the instrument.",
    "",
    "Try:",
    "  /start",
    "  /looper rec=on at=cycle   ...   /looper rec=off at=cycle",
    "  /looper morph=1 32b       the staircase resolves into normal playback",
    "  /oxide disint=on          the tape starts to shed; /oxide counts down (wear 0.1 ~ 2 min)",
    "  /mix gain=0 8b            hear only the loop wearing out",
    "  /oxide trim=3             the attendant brings the level back",
    "  /notverb freeze=on        catch a moment and hold it",
    "  /fbm depth=0.6 16b        more ecosystem",
    "  /deeppad excite=1 decay=0.3   the pad becomes a resonant processor"
  ],
